und" data-testid="ranking-stats">At the latest monthly read, 41,870 npm packages are used directly by at least one repository with 100+ stars. By weekly downloads, the top three are <a class="transition-colors duration-200 underline text-inherit hover:text-foreground" href="/package/npm/moss-date">moss-date</a> (5,806,310), <a class="transition-colors duration-200 underline text-inherit hover:text-foreground" href="/package/npm/@orbit/fetch">@orbit/fetch</a> (3,120,664) and <a class="transition-colors duration-200 underline text-inherit hover:text-foreground" href="/package/npm/kite-router">kite-router</a> (2,410,552). Only npm, only direct dependents, downloads to November 15, 2026. Ranks as of November 17, 2026. <a class="transition-colors duration-200 underline text-inherit hover:text-foreground" href="/methodology/packages">How package rankings work</a>.</p><section class="flex flex-col gap-4"><h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Questions</h2><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What does the npm package ranking by downloads count?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Rank is based on npm downloads in the 7 days to November 15, 2026. A package is ranked once at least one repository with 100+ stars uses it directly."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which npm package is first by weekly downloads?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"moss-date, with 5,806,310 downloads in the 7 days to November 15, 2026. Then @orbit/fetch and kite-router."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What counts as a dependent?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A public repository with 100+ stars that lists the package in its own package.json. Lockfiles, forks and example, docs or test folders don't count, and neither does a package that only comes in through another package."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How often are package rankings updated?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Dependents are read once a month, last on November 16, 2026. Ranks are worked out again after each monthly read and at least once a week; these are of November 17, 2026."}}]}</script><dl class="flex flex-col gap-4 text-sm"><div class="flex flex-col gap-1"><dt class="font-semibold">What does the npm package ranking by downloads count?</dt><dd class="text-muted-foreground">Rank is based on npm downloads in the 7 days to November 15, 2026. A package is ranked once at least one repository with 100+ stars uses it directly.</dd></div><div class="flex flex-col gap-1"><dt class="font-semibold">Which npm package is first by weekly downloads?</dt><dd class="text-muted-foreground">moss-date, with 5,806,310 downloads in the 7 days to November 15, 2026. Then @orbit/fetch and kite-router.</dd></div><div class="flex flex-col gap-1"><dt class="font-semibold">What counts as a dependent?</dt><dd class="text-muted-foreground">A public repository with 100+ stars that lists the package in its own package.json. Lockfiles, forks and example, docs or test folders don&#x27;t count, and neither does a package that only comes in through another package.</dd></div><div class="flex flex-col gap-1"><dt class="font-semibold">How often are package rankings updated?</dt><dd class="text-muted-foreground">Dependents are read once a month, last on November 16, 2026. Ranks are worked out again after each monthly read and at least once a week; these are of November 17, 2026.</dd></div></dl></section>"`;
